{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000101",
  "title": "Mandelbrot Set",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[dependencies]\nplotters = \"0.3\"\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Mandelbrot Set \ud83c\udf00\n\nThe **Mandelbrot set** is the most famous fractal in mathematics. It is defined as the set of complex numbers *c* for which the iteration\n\n> z_{n+1} = z_n\u00b2 + c,  starting with z\u2080 = 0\n\nremains bounded (|z| \u2264 2) as n \u2192 \u221e.\n\n## The Escape-Time Algorithm\n\nFor each pixel we map its position to a complex number *c*, then iterate the formula above. If |z| exceeds 2, the sequence will diverge \u2014 the number of iterations before escape determines the pixel's color. Points that never escape (up to our iteration limit) are colored black \u2014 these lie *inside* the Mandelbrot set.\n\nThe boundary is a fractal of infinite complexity: no matter how far you zoom in, there is always more detail.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Full Mandelbrot View",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Image and grid dimensions\nlet (width, height) = (800u32, 600u32);\nlet (cols, rows) = (200u32, 150u32);\nlet max_iter = 100u32;\n\n// Classic full view of the Mandelbrot set\nlet (x_min, x_max) = (-2.5_f64, 1.0);\nlet (y_min, y_max) = (-1.25_f64, 1.25);\n\n// Bernstein-polynomial color map: black interior,\n// smooth blue \u2192 teal \u2192 orange gradient outside\nfn color_map(n: u32, max_n: u32) -> RGBColor {\n    if n == max_n {\n        return RGBColor(0, 0, 0);\n    }\n    let t = n as f64 / max_n as f64;\n    RGBColor(\n        (9.0 * (1.0 - t) * t * t * t * 255.0) as u8,\n        (15.0 * (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t) * t * t * 255.0) as u8,\n        (8.5 * (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t) * t * 255.0) as u8,\n    )\n}\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (width, height))\n        .into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&BLACK).unwrap();\n\n    let cell_w = width / cols;\n    let cell_h = height / rows;\n\n    for row in 0..rows {\n        for col in 0..cols {\n            // Map grid cell to complex coordinate c\n            let cx = x_min + (col as f64 + 0.5) / cols as f64 * (x_max - x_min);\n            let cy = y_min + (row as f64 + 0.5) / rows as f64 * (y_max - y_min);\n\n            // Iterate z = z\u00b2 + c starting at z = 0\n            let (mut zx, mut zy) = (0.0_f64, 0.0_f64);\n            let mut n = 0u32;\n            while zx * zx + zy * zy <= 4.0 && n < max_iter {\n                let tmp = zx * zx - zy * zy + cx;\n                zy = 2.0 * zx * zy + cy;\n                zx = tmp;\n                n += 1;\n            }\n\n            let x0 = (col * cell_w) as i32;\n            let y0 = (row * cell_h) as i32;\n            root.draw(&Rectangle::new(\n                [(x0, y0), (x0 + cell_w as i32, y0 + cell_h as i32)],\n                color_map(n, max_iter).filled(),\n            ))\n            .unwrap();\n        }\n    }\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nSvg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_1\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Seahorse Valley Zoom",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Same rendering approach, zoomed into the \"seahorse valley\"\nlet (width, height) = (800u32, 600u32);\nlet (cols, rows) = (200u32, 150u32);\nlet max_iter = 200u32; // Higher limit reveals finer detail\n\n// Seahorse valley \u2014 a region of beautiful spirals\nlet (x_min, x_max) = (-0.77_f64, -0.73);\nlet (y_min, y_max) = (0.08_f64, 0.12);\n\nfn color_map(n: u32, max_n: u32) -> RGBColor {\n    if n == max_n {\n        return RGBColor(0, 0, 0);\n    }\n    let t = n as f64 / max_n as f64;\n    RGBColor(\n        (9.0 * (1.0 - t) * t * t * t * 255.0) as u8,\n        (15.0 * (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t) * t * t * 255.0) as u8,\n        (8.5 * (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t) * (1.0 - t) * t * 255.0) as u8,\n    )\n}\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (width, height))\n        .into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&BLACK).unwrap();\n\n    let cell_w = width / cols;\n    let cell_h = height / rows;\n\n    for row in 0..rows {\n        for col in 0..cols {\n            let cx = x_min + (col as f64 + 0.5) / cols as f64 * (x_max - x_min);\n            let cy = y_min + (row as f64 + 0.5) / rows as f64 * (y_max - y_min);\n\n            let (mut zx, mut zy) = (0.0_f64, 0.0_f64);\n            let mut n = 0u32;\n            while zx * zx + zy * zy <= 4.0 && n < max_iter {\n                let tmp = zx * zx - zy * zy + cx;\n                zy = 2.0 * zx * zy + cy;\n                zx = tmp;\n                n += 1;\n            }\n\n            let x0 = (col * cell_w) as i32;\n            let y0 = (row * cell_h) as i32;\n            root.draw(&Rectangle::new(\n                [(x0, y0), (x0 + cell_w as i32, y0 + cell_h as i32)],\n                color_map(n, max_iter).filled(),\n            ))\n            .unwrap();\n        }\n    }\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nSvg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_2\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_3",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Explore Further",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## \ud83d\udd0d Explore Further\n\nTry modifying the zoom parameters to explore other interesting regions:\n\n| Region | x range | y range |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| Elephant Valley | \\[0.25, 0.40\\] | \\[\u22120.10, 0.10\\] |\n| Spiral | \\[\u22120.088, \u22120.086\\] | \\[0.654, 0.656\\] |\n| Mini-brot | \\[\u22121.790, \u22121.780\\] | \\[\u22120.005, 0.005\\] |\n| Lightning | \\[\u22121.26, \u22121.24\\] | \\[0.04, 0.06\\] |\n\nIncrease `max_iter` for deeper zooms to reveal finer detail. The fractal is infinitely deep \u2014 you are limited only by floating-point precision!",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ]
}
